From 31af6ad709246aa9d43da34595dedd9abbf136e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 20:14:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] MEM2 step 1: the PS1's premade bios leave the EXE for SPU
 RAM (+45,776 B resident)

The 45 KB of premade citizens' bios (core/gen/roster_data.c) are no longer linked on
the PS1 (DOOMO_ROSTER_BIO_EXT). ps1/tools/rosterbin.py writes them as 64-byte records
to ROSTER.BIN; src/rosterbio.c uploads it to SPU RAM at 0x40000 at boot (below the part
store; the effects stop there, they use 35 KB), and roster_bio() reads one record back
with one 64-byte SPU DMA read into a ring of four (core/src/roster.c roster_bio_ext).
Same strings, same callers (each uses the bio at once). EXE with the boot FMV:
110,608 -> 156,384 B below the stack top. GBA, Dreamcast and native unchanged.

Tests: three native tests of roster_bio_ext (every bio equals the linked text; the four
newest stay valid without a read; a missing store reads empty and is not kept), four
rosterbin.py tests, game_smoke expects 'roster: bios loaded'.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RLcGbHBa2kju7ynbaJLHT6
